### ==========================================================
### TRANSACTIONS — crear, quick-add, ADJUSTMENT, idempotencia,
### filtros, tags, update, delete
### Crea sus propias cuentas/categoría arriba para ser autosuficiente.
### Las respuestas incluyen source (MANUAL/QUICK), currency y timestamps.
### ==========================================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = tester@test.com
@password = SecureP@ss123
@date = 2026-08-31T12:00:00.000Z

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###

@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Cuenta A (queda default si es la primera) — para EXPENSE/quick-add
# @name accA
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "TxA {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "CASH", "balance": 1000 }

###

@accAId = {{accA.response.body.id}}

### Cuenta B — destino de INCOME/TRANSFER
# @name accB
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "TxB {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "SAVINGS", "balance": 500 }

###

@accBId = {{accB.response.body.id}}

### Categoría para clasificar (el type debe coincidir con el de la transacción)
# @name cat
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "TxCat {{$randomInt 100 999}}", "type": "EXPENSE" }

###

@catId = {{cat.response.body.id}}

### ---------- Éxito ----------

### Crear EXPENSE (resta de A) — tags se normalizan (trim+minúsculas+dedupe)
# @name expense
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "EXPENSE",
  "amount": 42.50,
  "date": "{{date}}",
  "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}",
  "categoryId": "{{catId}}",
  "tags": ["Café ", "café", "hormiga"],
  "note": "prueba"
}

###

@txId = {{expense.response.body.id}}

### Crear INCOME (suma a B)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "INCOME", "amount": 300, "date": "{{date}}", "toAccountId": "{{accBId}}" }

### Crear TRANSFER (A -> B)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "TRANSFER", "amount": 100, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "toAccountId": "{{accBId}}" }

### ADJUSTMENT — reconciliar saldo: SUBE el saldo de B (toAccountId)
### Sin categoría; excluido de stats y budgets.
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "ADJUSTMENT", "amount": 12.34, "date": "{{date}}", "toAccountId": "{{accBId}}" }

### ADJUSTMENT — BAJA el saldo de A (fromAccountId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "ADJUSTMENT", "amount": 5, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Idempotencia — mismo Idempotency-Key + mismo body dos veces = una sola transacción
### Corre esta y la siguiente: deben devolver el MISMO id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 9.99, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Idempotencia — reintento con la misma clave (devuelve la existente)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 9.99, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Quick-add — solo amount (usa la cuenta default, marca pendingDetails y source=QUICK)
### También acepta Idempotency-Key (el flujo del doble-tap).
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/quick
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: quick-key-001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 5.25 }

### Bandeja de pendientes de detallar
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?pendingDetails=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Completar la bandeja en UNA petición (hasta 100 ítems)
### Cada ítem es independiente: si uno falla, los demás sí se guardan y el
### response trae `updated` y `failed` con el code de cada fallo. HTTP 200
### incluso con fallos: hay que leer `failed`, no el status.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/transactions/batch
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: batch-{{$randomInt 1000 9999}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "id": "{{txId}}", "categoryId": "{{catId}}", "description": "Detallado", "pendingDetails": false },
    { "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-999999999999", "description": "id inexistente -> failed" }
  ]
}

### Lote inválido — id repetido (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/transactions/batch
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "id": "{{txId}}", "description": "a" }, { "id": "{{txId}}", "description": "b" } ] }

### Bandeja + total en una sola petición (Inicio y la bandeja del diseño)
### includeSummary añade summary.totalAmount sobre TODO el conjunto filtrado,
### no sobre la página: con limit=1 devuelve el conteo y la suma sin traer filas.
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?pendingDetails=true&includeSummary=true&limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Listar (todas, orden por fecha desc)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por cuenta
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId={{accAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por categoría (drill-down desde stats/budgets)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?categoryId={{catId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por rango de fechas [from, to) — límites en la zona del usuario
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?from=2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z&to=2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por tag (normalizado: minúsculas)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?tag=café
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por origen — "Only quick entries" de la hoja de filtros
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?source=QUICK
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por origen — solo las creadas con el formulario completo
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?source=MANUAL
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Conteo anticipado del botón de la hoja de filtros: limit=1 y leer pagination.total
### (total respeta los filtros y NO depende de la página ni del cursor)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?source=QUICK&limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sin categoría (drill-down del bucket "uncategorized" de stats)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?uncategorized=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filtrar por tipo
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?type=EXPENSE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tags distintos del usuario (autocomplete)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/tags
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get por id
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update — cambia monto (revierte y reaplica balance; guarda revisión interna)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 60, "note": "editada" }

### Update solo nota/tags — NO toca balances (funciona aunque la cuenta esté archivada)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "solo metadatos" }

### Delete (soft) — revierte el efecto en el balance. SIN restore: si se
### necesita de nuevo, se crea otra.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Casos de error ----------

### Fecha futura >24h (400 FUTURE_DATE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 10, "date": "2030-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Idempotencia — misma clave con BODY DISTINTO (422 IDEMPOTENCY_PAYLOAD_MISMATCH)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 777, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Idempotency-Key inválida — charset/longitud (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: clave con espacios!!
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 1, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### ADJUSTMENT con ambos lados (400: exactamente uno)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "ADJUSTMENT", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "toAccountId": "{{accBId}}" }

### ADJUSTMENT con categoría (400: no admite categoryId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "ADJUSTMENT", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "categoryId": "{{catId}}" }

### Quick-add con type ADJUSTMENT (400: no permitido en quick)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/quick
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 10, "type": "ADJUSTMENT" }

### Categoría inexistente/ajena (404 Category not found)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "categoryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }

### Categoría de tipo contrario (400 CATEGORY_TYPE_MISMATCH) — catId es EXPENSE
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "INCOME", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "toAccountId": "{{accBId}}", "categoryId": "{{catId}}" }

### EXPENSE con toAccountId (no permitido) (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "toAccountId": "{{accBId}}" }

### INCOME sin toAccountId (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "INCOME", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}" }

### TRANSFER misma cuenta (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "TRANSFER", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "toAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Monto 0 (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 0, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### Monto con 3 decimales (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 10.555, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}" }

### fromAccountId de otro usuario / inexistente (404 uniforme)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 10, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }

### Cursor de paginación inválido (400 INVALID_CURSOR)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?cursor=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ==========================================================
### O-B1 — id del cliente (offline). Re-ejecutable: la segunda
### corrida responde 200 (replay) en vez de 201.
### ==========================================================

### Crear con id propio (201 la primera vez, 200 el replay)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000f1", "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 12.5, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "categoryId": "{{catId}}", "description": "Offline" }

### Replay idéntico (200, sin mover saldos otra vez)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000f1", "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 12.5, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "categoryId": "{{catId}}", "description": "Offline" }

### Mismo id, importe distinto (409 ID_TAKEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000f1", "type": "EXPENSE", "amount": 99, "date": "{{date}}", "fromAccountId": "{{accAId}}", "categoryId": "{{catId}}", "description": "Offline" }

### Quick-add con id propio (201 / 200 en el replay). El replay se juzga
### solo por lo que el cliente mandó: date y cuenta sin enviar resolverían
### a "ahora" y a la cuenta default del momento.
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/quick
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000f2", "amount": 7 }

### Replay del quick-add (200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/quick
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000f2", "amount": 7 }

### Mismo id, importe distinto (409 ID_TAKEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/quick
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "019a0000-0b01-7000-8000-0000000000f2", "amount": 8 }

### ==========================================================
### O-B2 — If-Match (concurrencia optimista). PATCH /transactions/batch
### NO lleva guarda: una cabecera no puede direccionar N documentos.
### ==========================================================

### Leer la transacción para quedarse con su updatedAt
# @name txForIfMatch
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

@txVersion = {{txForIfMatch.response.body.updatedAt}}

### Editar con la versión correcta (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{txVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Editada con If-Match" }

### La misma versión otra vez (409 STALE_UPDATE; `current` trae la transacción del servidor)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: {{txVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99 }

### Borrar con versión vieja (409 STALE_UPDATE, y el saldo NO se mueve)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/transactions/{{txId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
If-Match: 2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z
